                 <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and d=
evelopment news and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A    =
                      </mj-raw>=0D=0A                          <p>Finding t=
he typeface you need is a whole thing. <em>You=E2=80=99ll know it when you =
see it</em> is one approach. Look at a lot of choices. Make sure to save on=
es that you think are really nice, even if they aren=E2=80=99t the winner t=
his time. On my local machine, I use an app called <a href=3D"https://go.sp=
arkpostmail2.com/f/a/EHrDu0xGXHRrcaWcL175RA~~/AABEfhA~/BaQpriZ3Z8_bj-EAlyuF=
7jzv0RuXOxrn2BxmGMCF4JKlp-eOVMevUm4yaYgdY84uO1acU4VRBBA43tg9a9_3srxAX-ycGyo=
oYkNyHkOKBY9Zrh3-toKpI-5VIwwyRPoM">Typeface</a>. I try to tag stuff in cate=
gories that make sense to me. I have a good amount of nice stuff in there, =
but still, when looking for a web project, it=E2=80=99s limiting, because I=
 don=E2=80=99t have local versions of all the typefaces that would be good =
candidates for a web project. All of Google Fonts, for instance, I have no =
interest in keeping local copies of. And it=E2=80=99s extremely cost-prohib=
itive to buy every great font I see available for purchase.</p>=0A<p>I find=
 it interesting to look at ways to explore typefaces in novel ways. For ins=
tance, font.fish has a way to explore them in a big scrollable grid.</p>=0A=
<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-c=
gi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/font_explorer=
_cloud_corner1.png" alt=3D"Typefaces in a huge word cloud. " width=3D"450"/=
>=0A<p>As you explore clusters and axises, you can see how the groupings wo=
rk and perhaps find what you need by virtue of similarity and variation in =
what you need.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.co=
depenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepe=
n-spark/cloud_detail_corner2.png" alt=3D"Closer-in detail of the typeface w=
ord cloud, showing where different typefaces congregate together. " width=
=3D"450"/>=0A<p><a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/VdpKxB2kZ7Z8qY=
ta8JLWJg~~/AABEfhA~/lhe0MoU9dqHV9guGVo-jDOBOJsrSAFggRiUCGZYhtQDrhfF5RZJORIQ=
Q4C15Ru_YbLJW3JoEmnPaFESSfOQJVKvTe1tJyEmWkdVCgpPgUGBcDlqK8o_FypdRgzYX_iYW">=
Sweetfont</a> has a different approach where you move around on different a=
xises like from Loud to Quiet or from Playful to Formal. Then ultimately ju=
st see one particular font that fits the bill.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://pr=
oduction-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,q=
uality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/font_sliders_corner3.png" alt=3D"Th=
e control panels for selecting fonts to fit a mood, from Sweetfont. " width=
=3D"450"/>=0A<p>A more traditional way to organize fonts is to just make br=
oad relatable categories, like <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a=
/WYOv7Sw8E9dyTtyHIOy_ag~~/AABEfhA~/wfaNrWieLwTQz-R3noExOXXX6j0octzSZVkoFu_D=
iixBGgmVt6FNPvbMNPOK9me_0zBa-SnSiXzuRVpZ9rJxZJ9KLbWfrO16mo0KqaHUktT9SsZ8CBf=
QzrD0QXRtu96d">Typographer</a> does.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-c=
odepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D9=
0,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/type_categories_corner4.png" alt=3D"Type styl=
es organized into multiple categories, from Typographer. " width=3D"200"/>=
=0A<p>And to be fair, Google Fonts does have that, too. They=E2=80=99ve com=
e a long way.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.cod=
epenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen=
-spark/google_fonts_corner5.png" alt=3D"The font 'feeling' category option =
from Google Fonts. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>But nothing <em>sells</em> a font=
 like a good ol fashioned specimen page. It=E2=80=99s hard for me to look a=
t practical <em>any</em> specimen page and not be sold on it. For instance,=
 I=E2=80=99d love to work on a product that got to use <a href=3D"https://g=
o.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/Er3EJlsecxC1EiN2gPfW0g~~/AABEfhA~/Gsqbcvu8i5sOrt6u=
zyAnoXPHYvonRgoW_XUbYm4gvBhfSCQSiTJ7jNmnbUBt-dH8ePqNVdBcEktPsckbaE6fvvfyPWz=
Zi9Rn2VIuIFHBkWHW3xU5Mpfg40f4yfjKxCBc0FJRZ7eglYLdW6LmLLGfP3YyShdic86rqhd6dR=
cuYVM~">MD UI</a>.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-asset=
s.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/co=
depen-spark/specimen_pagecorner_6.png" alt=3D"Detail from the specimen page=
 for the MD UI typeface. It features it in use on transit signs, a smartwat=
ch, a settings dial, and a computer interface. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>Maybe=
